00:33:41,937 --> 00:33:43,771
<i>Stop filming! You can't film this!</i>

525
00:33:43,772 --> 00:33:46,482
<i>Stop filming!</i>

526
00:33:46,483 --> 00:33:47,776
[news channel audio fades]

527
00:33:49,319 --> 00:33:50,695
Mmm.

528
00:33:52,447 --> 00:33:53,656
[♪ music fades]

529
00:33:53,657 --> 00:33:55,157
CHASING THE TRUTH OF THAT DAY

530
00:33:55,158 --> 00:33:57,368
SPECIAL REPORT
ON JIN ISOO'S MURDER ALLEGATIONS

531
00:33:57,369 --> 00:33:58,661
[♪ tense, dramatic music playing]

532
00:33:58,662 --> 00:34:00,829
I stand before you again
after a long absence.

533
00:34:00,830 --> 00:34:02,331
Given the gravity of the case,

534
00:34:02,332 --> 00:34:05,709
I will personally lead
today's special broadcast.

535
00:34:05,710 --> 00:34:10,799
Last night, a man fell from a building
at a deserted construction site.

536
00:34:11,633 --> 00:34:13,968
To understand the full scope of this case,

537
00:34:13,969 --> 00:34:17,179
we must begin
with the murder of Kim Younghwan.

538
00:34:17,180 --> 00:34:20,474
Ten days ago, Mr. Kim Younghwan,
the CEO of a film production company,

539
00:34:20,475 --> 00:34:22,018
was brutally murdered.

540
00:34:22,852 --> 00:34:25,813
The prime suspect was
the victim's close friend

541
00:34:25,814 --> 00:34:28,190
and the only person present at the scene,

542
00:34:28,191 --> 00:34:29,776
Detective Jin Isoo.

543
00:34:30,694 --> 00:34:32,486
There was compelling evidence,

544
00:34:32,487 --> 00:34:35,447
but Detective Jin was released
without charge a few days later.

545
00:34:35,448 --> 00:34:36,865
[Mujin] I thought it was unjust.

546
00:34:36,866 --> 00:34:40,077
All the evidence pointed to him,
but he was released without charge.

547
00:34:40,078 --> 00:34:43,289
I still think Jin Isoo is the killer.

548
00:34:43,290 --> 00:34:47,084
Gangha Violent Crime next arrested
a new suspect, Mr. Cho.

549
00:34:47,085 --> 00:34:48,961
However, in just a day,

550
00:34:48,962 --> 00:34:52,089
he was poisoned to death while in custody.

551
00:34:52,090 --> 00:34:53,882
Finally, last night,

552
00:34:53,883 --> 00:34:56,593
a new suspect, Mr. Hwang,

553
00:34:56,594 --> 00:34:59,097
fell to his death
while fleeing from police.

554
00:34:59,764 --> 00:35:02,641
Can we really call this a coincidence?

555
00:35:02,642 --> 00:35:06,562
Some speculate that in an attempt
to divert suspicion from himself,

556
00:35:06,563 --> 00:35:09,773
Detective Jin tried to frame Mr. Hwang,

557
00:35:09,774 --> 00:35:12,986
who has no connection to this case,
as a new suspect.

558
00:35:15,155 --> 00:35:16,156
Was his hand

559
00:35:17,907 --> 00:35:20,451
reaching out to save him?

560
00:35:20,452 --> 00:35:22,996
<i>Or was it to push him?</i>

561
00:35:25,749 --> 00:35:26,875
[♪ music fades]

562
00:35:27,626 --> 00:35:28,835
- [TV beeps]
- [remote clatters]

563
00:35:31,296 --> 00:35:34,298
She's spouting
whatever nonsense she wants.

564
00:35:34,299 --> 00:35:36,551
She stepped in herself
as a former news anchor.

565
00:35:38,595 --> 00:35:39,596
[sighs in exasperation]

566
00:35:44,976 --> 00:35:46,061
By the way,

567
00:35:49,105 --> 00:35:50,606
how did Hwang Jongsu know?

568
00:35:50,607 --> 00:35:52,524
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

569
00:35:52,525 --> 00:35:54,527
It looked like he was running away.

570
00:35:55,779 --> 00:35:58,073
How did he know that we suspected him?

571
00:36:07,832 --> 00:36:08,833
[♪ music fades]

572
00:36:12,921 --> 00:36:13,963
Team 1.

573
00:36:17,550 --> 00:36:21,095
Effective immediately,
you are all suspended.

574
00:36:21,096 --> 00:36:23,138
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

575
00:36:23,139 --> 00:36:25,767
Joo Hyera, do you have something to say?

576
00:36:30,647 --> 00:36:34,359
The suspect in Kim Younghwan's murder case
died while in custody,

577
00:36:35,735 --> 00:36:38,862
<i>a victim's dead body was delivered here,</i>

578
00:36:38,863 --> 00:36:42,909
and the suspect in that murder
committed suicide.

579
00:36:43,743 --> 00:36:44,910
[Taegyun sighs wearily]

580
00:36:44,911 --> 00:36:48,415
You deserve to be suspended, don't you?

581
00:36:58,341 --> 00:36:59,634
[♪ music increases in tempo]

582
00:37:00,802 --> 00:37:01,969
Get lost, all of you!

583
00:37:01,970 --> 00:37:03,972
Stay out of my sight!

584
00:37:06,141 --> 00:37:07,225
[swears softly]

585
00:37:08,309 --> 00:37:09,394
[mutters]

586
00:37:12,605 --> 00:37:13,815
[door opens]

587
00:37:17,110 --> 00:37:18,318
Chief.

588
00:37:18,319 --> 00:37:19,487
[sighs softly]

589
00:37:20,405 --> 00:37:21,864
Just stand down for now.

590
00:37:21,865 --> 00:37:23,323
- But--
- Hyera.

591
00:37:23,324 --> 00:37:26,034
If you keep this up,
you could lose your job.

592
00:37:26,035 --> 00:37:28,288
How will you catch
Yu Seongwon as a civilian?

593
00:37:30,540 --> 00:37:31,583
[sighs softly]

594
00:37:39,340 --> 00:37:40,592
[♪ music swells, fades]

595
00:37:42,802 --> 00:37:43,928
[knocking at door]

596
00:37:44,471 --> 00:37:45,472
Come in.

597
00:37:50,018 --> 00:37:52,854
- [door closes]
- I don't think it's even been 10 minutes

598
00:37:53,605 --> 00:37:55,815
since I told you to stay out of my sight.

599
00:37:56,441 --> 00:37:58,693
I'm here to make your wish come true, sir.

600
00:38:01,279 --> 00:38:02,280
[grunts softly]

601
00:38:06,743 --> 00:38:07,786
[clacks]

602
00:38:10,955 --> 00:38:12,414
LETTER OF RESIGNATION

603
00:38:12,415 --> 00:38:14,334
- [hand thuds on table]
- [exhales softly]

604
00:38:15,502 --> 00:38:16,503
I'll leave.

605
00:38:18,171 --> 00:38:19,589
That's your wish, isn't it?

606
00:38:20,924 --> 00:38:25,093
So leave Detective Joo,
Detective Park, and Detective Choi alone.

607
00:38:25,094 --> 00:38:26,303
[scoffs]

608
00:38:26,304 --> 00:38:28,181
They're already done for.

609
00:38:28,807 --> 00:38:30,892
There's going to be
a disciplinary hearing.

610
00:38:31,518 --> 00:38:32,936
You can all leave hand in hand.

611
00:38:35,855 --> 00:38:37,732
What exactly did we do wrong?

612
00:38:39,192 --> 00:38:41,945
If anyone did anything wrong here,
it wasn't us.

613
00:38:43,696 --> 00:38:45,239
It was you, sir.

614
00:38:45,240 --> 00:38:47,075
[♪ gripping, dramatic music playing]

615
00:38:49,118 --> 00:38:52,163
When we went,
Hwang Jongsu was already on the run.

616
00:38:52,831 --> 00:38:54,791
As if he had already been warned.

617
00:38:58,837 --> 00:39:00,754
I checked at the security office.

618
00:39:00,755 --> 00:39:02,465
GANGHA POLICE STATION SECURITY OFFICE

619
00:39:17,105 --> 00:39:18,439
<i>Who did you call?</i>

620
00:39:20,108 --> 00:39:23,026
It was just a work call.

621
00:39:23,027 --> 00:39:24,028
[Isoo] Sir.

622
00:39:25,363 --> 00:39:26,906
Do you know who Hwang Jongsu is?

623
00:39:28,324 --> 00:39:30,201
He's Yu Seongwon's closest associate.

624
00:39:31,160 --> 00:39:33,705
He's protected Yu Seongwon
since Seongwon was a child.

625
00:39:34,497 --> 00:39:37,333
If we're right and Yu Seongwon
committed murder in his studio,

626
00:39:38,543 --> 00:39:41,379
Hwang Jongsu is both a witness
to everything and an accomplice.

627
00:39:44,465 --> 00:39:46,217
Now do you understand what you did?

628
00:39:48,970 --> 00:39:50,889
You leaked confidential information.

629
00:39:51,890 --> 00:39:53,057
If you touch my team,

630
00:39:54,767 --> 00:39:56,101
I'm going to expose it.

631
00:39:56,102 --> 00:39:57,312
[♪ music swells]

632
00:40:05,236 --> 00:40:06,446
- [♪ music fades]
- [sighs]

633
00:40:08,072 --> 00:40:09,198
[Kyungjin sighs heavily]

634
00:40:12,285 --> 00:40:13,286
[sighs defeatedly]

635
00:40:16,623 --> 00:40:17,916
[♪ somber music playing]

636
00:40:26,174 --> 00:40:27,216
[sighs heavily]

637
00:40:31,763 --> 00:40:32,805
Detective Joo.

638
00:40:33,681 --> 00:40:34,682
What do we do now?

639
00:40:36,309 --> 00:40:37,392
[inhales deeply]

640
00:40:37,393 --> 00:40:39,145
You'll be fine.

641
00:40:39,729 --> 00:40:41,063
I'll find a way to stop it.

642
00:40:41,064 --> 00:40:44,441
Hey, you're a detective.
This can happen while working a case.

643
00:40:44,442 --> 00:40:45,818
No, that's not what I meant.

644
00:40:46,694 --> 00:40:47,987
How do we catch Yu Seongwon?

645
00:40:50,281 --> 00:40:52,575
The suspect's dead, and we're suspended.

646
00:40:53,284 --> 00:40:54,911
Yu Seongwon won't stop.

647
00:40:58,164 --> 00:40:59,624
What if he kills someone again?

648
00:41:02,043 --> 00:41:03,252
- [sighs wearily]
- [door opens]

649
00:41:04,504 --> 00:41:06,589
Why is everyone so down, huh?

650
00:41:07,548 --> 00:41:09,800
What's this? You're clocking out already?

651
00:41:09,801 --> 00:41:11,469
Unpack and get back to work.

652
00:41:12,136 --> 00:41:13,387
I'm the only one leaving.

653
00:41:13,388 --> 00:41:14,888
- What?
- What?

654
00:41:14,889 --> 00:41:16,223
What are you talking about?

655
00:41:16,224 --> 00:41:17,892
I made a deal with the police chief.

656
00:41:18,559 --> 00:41:20,436
I'm the one he hates most.

657
00:41:21,396 --> 00:41:22,605
I'll leave,

658
00:41:23,398 --> 00:41:24,857
and you three won't be suspended.

659
00:41:25,441 --> 00:41:26,900
[♪ gentle, somber music playing]

660
00:41:26,901 --> 00:41:28,360
[sighs] Jin Isoo.

661
00:41:28,361 --> 00:41:30,362
You guys don't have anywhere to go.

662
00:41:30,363 --> 00:41:32,240
I've got plenty of other options.

663
00:41:35,076 --> 00:41:36,077
Bro.

664
00:41:37,620 --> 00:41:39,580
- Are you really going to quit?
- Yes.

665
00:41:40,331 --> 00:41:42,792
I just went ahead
and handed the chief my resignation.

666
00:41:43,835 --> 00:41:45,043
[Junyoung] Hey.

667
00:41:45,044 --> 00:41:47,422
What do you think you're doing?

668
00:41:49,007 --> 00:41:50,883
This case started because of me.

669
00:41:51,718 --> 00:41:53,803
The press will come after me, too.

670
00:41:54,637 --> 00:41:56,097
Staying will only make it harder.

671
00:41:59,350 --> 00:42:00,684
I'll clear this up later.

672
00:42:00,685 --> 00:42:03,062
Take care. I'm a free man now.

673
00:42:05,023 --> 00:42:06,190
[door opens]

674
00:42:07,316 --> 00:42:08,484
- [door closes]
- [sighs softly]

675
00:42:11,946 --> 00:42:14,072
[Hyera panting]

676
00:42:14,073 --> 00:42:15,158
Jin Isoo.

677
00:42:17,285 --> 00:42:18,745
[continues panting]

678
00:42:20,955 --> 00:42:22,123
I'm sorry.

679
00:42:25,001 --> 00:42:26,919
Why do you look so defeated?

680
00:42:28,629 --> 00:42:30,840
I'll go out and do what I can
on the outside.

681
00:42:31,507 --> 00:42:32,508
You should

682
00:42:33,843 --> 00:42:35,261
hold things down here.

683
00:42:41,976 --> 00:42:43,853
I'm not giving up on Yu Seongwon.

684
00:42:44,437 --> 00:42:45,938
I'll catch him no matter what.

685
00:42:48,649 --> 00:42:49,817
[♪ music fades]

686
00:42:57,116 --> 00:42:58,825
Mr. Jin Isoo is here.

687
00:42:58,826 --> 00:43:00,369
Hello!

688
00:43:01,871 --> 00:43:03,663
Are you here to complain?

689
00:43:03,664 --> 00:43:06,041
No, I came to thank you.

690
00:43:06,042 --> 00:43:08,044
I'm a civilian now, thanks to you.

691
00:43:09,420 --> 00:43:10,880
I quit being a cop.

692
00:43:11,881 --> 00:43:14,341
You even went on the air
to give a special broadcast,

693
00:43:14,342 --> 00:43:16,177
and I got absolutely roasted.

694
00:43:17,220 --> 00:43:19,180
So I thought I'd bring you a gift.

695
00:43:20,014 --> 00:43:21,015
Here.

696
00:43:25,478 --> 00:43:28,063
Go on, open it.
I went to all this trouble.

697
00:43:28,064 --> 00:43:29,190
[clicks tongue]

698
00:43:31,442 --> 00:43:32,734
[♪ tense, pulsating music playing]

699
00:43:32,735 --> 00:43:34,319
It's custom-made.

700
00:43:34,320 --> 00:43:35,738
[chuckling]

701
00:43:37,865 --> 00:43:38,990
Is this gold?

702
00:43:38,991 --> 00:43:40,283
Yes.

703
00:43:40,284 --> 00:43:42,410
One for you, one for Seongwon.

704
00:43:42,411 --> 00:43:45,623
If you ever want to turn yourself in,
wear that to Gangha Police Station.

705
00:43:46,499 --> 00:43:50,127
[sighs] Chairman Jin Myeongchul
was a good man,

706
00:43:50,128 --> 00:43:51,336
but his son's a letdown.

707
00:43:51,337 --> 00:43:53,965
You should worry about your own son.

708
00:43:54,757 --> 00:43:56,801
How did you bring him up to be a murderer?

709
00:43:59,846 --> 00:44:01,347
Nothing's holding me back now.

710
00:44:02,014 --> 00:44:04,558
Being a detective
comes with a lot of restrictions.

711
00:44:04,559 --> 00:44:08,020
I need to play by the rules
and keep the brass happy.

712
00:44:08,604 --> 00:44:09,856
I don't have that anymore.

713
00:44:12,024 --> 00:44:13,109
[scoffs]

714
00:44:14,026 --> 00:44:17,404
Just watch and see how far I can go.

715
00:44:17,405 --> 00:44:18,948
[♪ music increases in tempo]

716
00:44:24,620 --> 00:44:25,955
[♪ music swells]

717
00:44:30,418 --> 00:44:31,710
[♪ music resumes tempo]

718
00:44:31,711 --> 00:44:32,712
[door slams]

719
00:44:33,462 --> 00:44:34,505
[scoffs softly]

720
00:44:35,923 --> 00:44:37,008
[♪ music fades]

721
00:44:41,971 --> 00:44:43,681
Are you busy, Mr. Chairman?

722
00:44:44,390 --> 00:44:46,267
[exhales incredulously]
What brings you here?

723
00:44:47,226 --> 00:44:48,728
You were eating.

724
00:44:49,312 --> 00:44:50,396
[Mr. Choi sighs softly]

725
00:44:52,732 --> 00:44:54,483
Are you here because of the broadcast?

726
00:44:55,443 --> 00:44:57,903
I filed a correction
with the arbitration commission.

727
00:44:57,904 --> 00:44:59,363
They won't listen.

728
00:44:59,906 --> 00:45:00,907
What?

729
00:45:02,533 --> 00:45:03,826
Chairwoman Jeong Taeseon

730
00:45:04,827 --> 00:45:06,120
was just using me.

731
00:45:07,538 --> 00:45:08,622
Why?

732
00:45:08,623 --> 00:45:11,708
- Because her son is a killer...
- [gasps]

733
00:45:11,709 --> 00:45:13,335
...and I'm going to catch him.

734
00:45:13,336 --> 00:45:15,420
What are you talking about?

735
00:45:15,421 --> 00:45:18,674
The artist Yu Seongwon is a killer?

736
00:45:19,342 --> 00:45:22,260
Yes, a serial killer.

737
00:45:22,261 --> 00:45:24,596
So I got fired today.

738
00:45:24,597 --> 00:45:25,680
What?

739
00:45:25,681 --> 00:45:26,765
I'm unemployed.

740
00:45:26,766 --> 00:45:28,016
[♪ upbeat, jaunty music playing]

741
00:45:28,017 --> 00:45:30,894
I did give in my resignation,
but I was basically fired.

742
00:45:30,895 --> 00:45:34,273
Then what are you going to do?

743
00:45:35,399 --> 00:45:36,817
[Isoo] Mmm...

744
00:45:38,486 --> 00:45:39,487
Mr. Choi.

745
00:45:40,696 --> 00:45:42,573
Don't we have some white hackers here?

746
00:45:43,157 --> 00:45:46,285
We don't have any on staff,
but we have people under contract.

747
00:45:47,078 --> 00:45:48,079
Set me up with them.

748
00:45:49,330 --> 00:45:53,000
I'm going to arrest
Yu Seongwon and Jeong Taeseon both.

749
00:45:53,584 --> 00:45:57,004
All right. I'll give them a call.

750
00:45:58,005 --> 00:45:59,006
Ah.

751
00:45:59,507 --> 00:46:01,466
Our subsidiaries advertise on UBS, right?

752
00:46:01,467 --> 00:46:02,884
Cancel everything.

753
00:46:02,885 --> 00:46:04,678
I'm going to sue for defamation.

754
00:46:04,679 --> 00:46:05,721
[scoffs]

755
00:46:07,348 --> 00:46:09,725
- Is that sushi?
- What? Oh.

756
00:46:10,351 --> 00:46:11,519
[♪ music fades]

757
00:46:12,103 --> 00:46:13,896
- [chuckles]
- [sighs contentedly]

758
00:46:14,230 --> 00:46:16,148
[♪ upbeat rock music playing]

759
00:46:18,567 --> 00:46:20,111
[engine purring smoothly]

760
00:46:46,345 --> 00:46:47,346
Mmm!

761
00:46:48,180 --> 00:46:49,348
Detective Jin Isoo!

762
00:46:50,683 --> 00:46:52,600
- I'm a fan.
- Right.

763
00:46:52,601 --> 00:46:54,020
[♪ music fades]

764
00:46:54,478 --> 00:46:55,479
Really?

765
00:46:57,815 --> 00:46:59,025
Yes.

766
00:46:59,817 --> 00:47:01,402
Did you really kill Kim Younghwan?

767
00:47:02,153 --> 00:47:03,236
No.

768
00:47:03,237 --> 00:47:05,740
Oh, if you did, that'd be a killer story.

769
00:47:06,449 --> 00:47:08,199
Can you stop talking about killing?

770
00:47:08,200 --> 00:47:10,160
I heard you had a request for us.

771
00:47:10,161 --> 00:47:11,162
Yes.

772
00:47:12,913 --> 00:47:14,081
Find this person for me.

773
00:47:14,874 --> 00:47:18,668
I think he's a close associate
of UBS's Jeong Taeseon.

774
00:47:18,669 --> 00:47:20,462
He could be a former employee.

775
00:47:20,463 --> 00:47:22,464
I can't find him in the company records.

776
00:47:22,465 --> 00:47:24,382
Did this guy kill Kim Younghwan?

777
00:47:24,383 --> 00:47:25,508
No.

778
00:47:25,509 --> 00:47:27,469
[♪ jaunty, suspenseful music playing]

779
00:47:27,470 --> 00:47:28,846
But he is a murderer.

780
00:47:29,930 --> 00:47:32,098
He killed the guy
who killed Kim Younghwan.

781
00:47:32,099 --> 00:47:34,351
- Oh!
- Oh! [chuckling]

782
00:47:34,352 --> 00:47:35,727
[scoffs]

783
00:47:35,728 --> 00:47:37,521
Can you find him without a name?

784
00:47:38,564 --> 00:47:39,690
- Of course!
- Of course!

785
00:47:40,733 --> 00:47:43,569
But before that, can I get your autograph?

786
00:47:44,278 --> 00:47:45,403
Me too.

787
00:47:45,404 --> 00:47:46,530
[♪ music fades]

788
00:47:47,114 --> 00:47:48,990
[scoffs] Bring me a pen.

789
00:47:48,991 --> 00:47:50,992
[♪ driving rock music playing]

790
00:47:50,993 --> 00:47:52,995
JIN ISOO

791
00:47:55,289 --> 00:47:56,457
JIN ISOO

792
00:48:03,631 --> 00:48:05,257
DIRECTOR KIM IS HERE

793
00:48:12,264 --> 00:48:13,390
[♪ music turns suspenseful]

794
00:48:13,391 --> 00:48:15,393
[Taeseon's adviser]
<i>Hansu pulled all their advertising.</i>

795
00:48:17,311 --> 00:48:19,104
I know. I heard.

796
00:48:19,105 --> 00:48:20,897
They're even threatening a lawsuit.

797
00:48:20,898 --> 00:48:22,315
We should issue a correction.

798
00:48:22,316 --> 00:48:24,109
No, just leave it.

799
00:48:24,110 --> 00:48:25,235
Pardon?

800
00:48:25,236 --> 00:48:27,988
I said leave it. I'll handle it!

801
00:48:28,572 --> 00:48:29,864
Yes, ma'am.

802
00:48:29,865 --> 00:48:31,659
[♪ tense, pulsating music playing]

803
00:48:36,789 --> 00:48:37,998
[♪ music swells]

804
00:48:39,500 --> 00:48:40,667
[♪ music fades]

805
00:48:40,668 --> 00:48:43,711
RETURN II
YU SEONGWON'S SOLO EXHIBITION

806
00:48:43,712 --> 00:48:45,255
[director] Mr. Yu, welcome.

807
00:48:45,256 --> 00:48:47,173
Yes, hello.

808
00:48:47,174 --> 00:48:50,176
You're as handsome as always.
Have you been well?

809
00:48:50,177 --> 00:48:51,887
Yes. I hope you've been well, too.

810
00:48:52,471 --> 00:48:54,931
I've been so busy
getting the exhibition ready.

811
00:48:54,932 --> 00:48:56,934
Come this way. We've set up the pieces.

812
00:49:05,276 --> 00:49:06,777
What do you think?

813
00:49:09,697 --> 00:49:11,532
[♪ tense, ominous music playing]

814
00:49:12,783 --> 00:49:14,243
For this exhibition,

815
00:49:18,873 --> 00:49:20,541
that is the main piece.

816
00:49:23,169 --> 00:49:26,755
It needs to be the first thing
people see when they walk in.

817
00:49:27,715 --> 00:49:28,799
So vivid,

818
00:49:29,758 --> 00:49:32,135
it almost seems alive.

819
00:49:32,136 --> 00:49:33,387
FULL BLOOM, LIFE YET TO BLOOM

820
00:49:36,098 --> 00:49:37,099
You get what I mean?

821
00:49:37,892 --> 00:49:39,185
[chuckles softly] Yes.

822
00:49:40,311 --> 00:49:41,479
[cell phone vibrating]

823
00:49:45,274 --> 00:49:47,400
JEONG TAESEON

824
00:49:47,401 --> 00:49:48,611
[sighs in exasperation]

825
00:49:50,446 --> 00:49:52,740
- [Taeseon] <i>Come to the office right now.
-</i> [line disconnects]

826
00:49:57,703 --> 00:49:58,704
[♪ music fades]

827
00:49:59,330 --> 00:50:00,372
[door closes]

828
00:50:00,998 --> 00:50:02,290
[inhales sharply]

829
00:50:02,291 --> 00:50:03,750
We're meeting too often lately.

830
00:50:03,751 --> 00:50:05,251
[muffled footsteps]

831
00:50:05,252 --> 00:50:07,379
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

832
00:50:08,255 --> 00:50:10,174
I've got a plane ready,
so leave right now.

833
00:50:14,637 --> 00:50:16,889
I can't cover for you any more than this.

834
00:50:19,058 --> 00:50:22,018
If they look into Mr. Hwang,
everything will link back to you.

835
00:50:22,019 --> 00:50:23,394
Then there's nothing I can do.

836
00:50:23,395 --> 00:50:25,146
[♪ suspenseful, pulsating music playing]

837
00:50:25,147 --> 00:50:27,399
<i>Just stay out until I clean everything up.</i>

838
00:50:29,360 --> 00:50:31,445
I'm asking you.

839
00:50:32,112 --> 00:50:33,405
Please!

840
00:50:42,456 --> 00:50:44,333
If you really want it, then beg me.

841
00:50:49,755 --> 00:50:51,215
[chuckling smugly]

842
00:50:52,091 --> 00:50:53,092
Okay, fine.

843
00:50:54,009 --> 00:50:56,470
It was a joke.

844
00:50:58,222 --> 00:50:59,223
Fine.

845
00:51:00,766 --> 00:51:01,767
<i>I'll leave.</i>

846
00:51:03,811 --> 00:51:04,978
[♪ music increases in tempo]

847
00:51:04,979 --> 00:51:08,398
Okay, find out when and where
UBS' private jet is leaving today.

848
00:51:08,399 --> 00:51:09,775
- Okay.
- Okay.

849
00:51:13,696 --> 00:51:16,240
- [keyboard key clacks]
- [rapid digital beeping]

850
00:51:17,074 --> 00:51:18,534
[digital beeps]

851
00:51:19,326 --> 00:51:21,202
In two hours. Business aviation terminal.

852
00:51:21,203 --> 00:51:22,705
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

853
00:51:24,873 --> 00:51:26,208
[cell phone vibrating]

854
00:51:28,919 --> 00:51:29,920
Hello?

855
00:51:30,754 --> 00:51:32,840
Yu Seongwon is flying out in two hours.

856
00:51:33,382 --> 00:51:34,465
Where is he going?

857
00:51:34,466 --> 00:51:37,261
[Isoo] <i>I don't know,
but he's flying on a private jet.</i>

858
00:51:38,429 --> 00:51:40,013
<i>Just go arrest him.</i>

859
00:51:40,014 --> 00:51:41,097
What will you do?

860
00:51:41,098 --> 00:51:45,310
Dr. Seo said Yu Seongwon
would have kept all the evidence.

861
00:51:45,311 --> 00:51:47,478
I'll go to his studio to find them.

862
00:51:47,479 --> 00:51:48,731
[♪ music swells]

863
00:51:49,773 --> 00:51:50,941
[♪ music fades]

864
00:51:52,526 --> 00:51:53,610
Get ready to move out.

865
00:51:53,611 --> 00:51:55,528
- Yes, ma'am.
- Yes, ma'am.

866
00:51:55,529 --> 00:51:57,072
[♪ suspenseful, foreboding music playing]

867
00:52:04,705 --> 00:52:05,998
[engine purring smoothly]

868
00:52:09,209 --> 00:52:10,376
[tires screech]

869
00:52:10,377 --> 00:52:11,795
[♪ music increases in tempo]

870
00:52:17,468 --> 00:52:18,802
[♪ music swells]

871
00:52:23,682 --> 00:52:24,683
[♪ music fades]

872
00:52:26,393 --> 00:52:27,978
[distant jet engine roaring]

873
00:52:29,104 --> 00:52:30,898
[♪ tense, ominous music playing]

874
00:52:35,194 --> 00:52:36,236
[♪ music fades]

875
00:52:41,158 --> 00:52:43,243
[♪ suspenseful, foreboding music playing]

876
00:52:46,455 --> 00:52:47,456
[hammer clangs]

877
00:53:13,816 --> 00:53:15,067
[♪ music increases in tempo]

878
00:53:26,328 --> 00:53:27,538
[♪ music resumes tempo]

879
00:53:38,090 --> 00:53:39,508
[♪ music increases in tempo]

880
00:53:56,442 --> 00:53:57,735
[creaking]

881
00:54:03,073 --> 00:54:04,491
[♪ music turns ominous]

882
00:54:30,142 --> 00:54:31,809
- [switch clicks]
- [light beeps]

883
00:54:31,810 --> 00:54:33,562
[lights beep sequentially]

884
00:55:03,926 --> 00:55:05,594
ECSTASY
A BREATHLESS FALL

885
00:55:10,390 --> 00:55:12,059
JO NAYEONG
YU SEONGWON'S MODEL

886
00:55:27,741 --> 00:55:29,659
CHOI YEONGMIN
YU SEONGWON'S MODEL

887
00:55:29,660 --> 00:55:31,578
CLIMAX
LIGHT SCATTERED ACROSS THE UNIVERSE

888
00:55:44,883 --> 00:55:47,802
[Isoo] <i>What's with the pebbles
and why stick the reed in?</i>

889
00:55:47,803 --> 00:55:49,680
DISSOLUTION
THE SILENCE OF WHISPERING REEDS

890
00:55:51,515 --> 00:55:52,683
KIM HEEJUN
YU SEONGWON'S JUNIOR

891
00:55:56,853 --> 00:55:58,188
[♪ music swells]

892
00:56:03,610 --> 00:56:05,404
FULL BLOOM, LIFE YET TO BLOOM

893
00:56:07,489 --> 00:56:10,074
[♪ ominous chord swells, fades]

894
00:56:10,075 --> 00:56:11,368
[♪ music resumes tempo]

895
00:56:17,249 --> 00:56:18,959
JEONG MINJAE
FORMER DETECTIVE

896
00:56:32,389 --> 00:56:33,640
[line connects, ringing]

897
00:56:34,600 --> 00:56:36,602
- [siren blaring]
- [cell phone vibrating]

898
00:56:38,270 --> 00:56:39,770
[Isoo] <i>It's me.</i>

899
00:56:39,771 --> 00:56:42,149
<i>I found Yu Seongwon's real studio.</i>

900
00:56:42,899 --> 00:56:45,276
All the evidence is here.

901
00:56:45,277 --> 00:56:47,362
[♪ suspenseful, pulsating music playing]

902
00:56:49,865 --> 00:56:50,949
He found the evidence.

903
00:56:57,539 --> 00:56:59,374
- [engine revving]
- [tires screeching]

904
00:57:00,959 --> 00:57:02,461
[line connects, ringing]

905
00:57:04,212 --> 00:57:06,798
Chief, I'm inside Yu Seongwon's studio.

906
00:57:07,382 --> 00:57:08,967
<i>There's a basement here.</i>

907
00:57:09,593 --> 00:57:13,221
I found the victims' belongings
and photographic evidence.

908
00:57:13,930 --> 00:57:15,931
I'll send Forensics over, so wait there.

909
00:57:15,932 --> 00:57:16,933
<i>Yes, sir.</i>

910
00:57:17,601 --> 00:57:18,727
[music stops]

911
00:57:20,646 --> 00:57:22,731
[♪ gripping, foreboding music playing]

912
00:57:41,541 --> 00:57:43,418
- [engine roaring]
- [siren approaching]

913
00:57:45,128 --> 00:57:46,462
[tires screech]

914
00:57:46,463 --> 00:57:47,756
- [siren stops]
- [♪ music swells]

915
00:57:48,674 --> 00:57:49,716
[♪ music fades]

916
00:57:51,677 --> 00:57:52,719
[scoffs]

917
00:57:53,679 --> 00:57:55,263
Are you here to say goodbye?

918
00:57:56,390 --> 00:57:59,350
Or have you grown attached to me?

919
00:57:59,351 --> 00:58:01,269
[♪ gripping, ominous music playing]

920
00:58:04,815 --> 00:58:06,942
- [Hyera] Yu Seongwon.
- [handcuffs clicking]

921
00:58:08,819 --> 00:58:11,320
For the murders
of Jo Nayeong, Choi Yeongmin,

922
00:58:11,321 --> 00:58:14,156
Kim Heejun, and Jeong Minjae...

923
00:58:14,157 --> 00:58:16,242
[♪ melancholy piano music playing]

924
00:58:16,243 --> 00:58:17,911
I am placing you under arrest.

925
00:58:20,330 --> 00:58:21,498
[chuckles softly]

926
00:58:22,999 --> 00:58:24,543
You sound confident.

927
00:58:26,253 --> 00:58:27,879
Is it for certain this time?

928
00:58:29,923 --> 00:58:31,383
Are you really sure

929
00:58:32,843 --> 00:58:34,302
you can catch me?

930
00:58:55,240 --> 00:58:57,199
[♪ ominous sting plays, fades]

931
00:58:57,200 --> 00:58:58,784
RESIDENT REGISTRATION CARD

932
00:58:58,785 --> 00:59:00,620
[♪ melancholy piano music continues]

933
00:59:02,748 --> 00:59:04,791
JIN ISOO

934
00:59:15,343 --> 00:59:17,219
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

935
00:59:17,220 --> 00:59:19,263
WHAT I HAD DRAWN WASN'T A HAT

936
00:59:19,264 --> 00:59:22,224
YOU ALWAYS HAVE TO EXPLAIN
EVERYTHING TO GROWN-UPS

937
00:59:22,225 --> 00:59:23,727
[cell phone vibrating]

938
00:59:32,652 --> 00:59:33,862
We got him.

939
00:59:34,654 --> 00:59:35,655
Okay.

940
00:59:36,573 --> 00:59:37,699
I'll be there soon.

941
00:59:47,375 --> 00:59:50,669
[Seongwon] <i>After all,
you're my Little Prince.</i>

942
00:59:50,670 --> 00:59:51,838
[♪ music slows]

943
00:59:53,715 --> 00:59:56,009
[♪ pulsating foreboding music playing]

944
01:00:06,770 --> 01:00:07,896
[exhales softly]

945
01:00:10,732 --> 01:00:12,149
Where is Isoo right now?

946
01:00:12,150 --> 01:00:13,777
[♪ music increases in tempo]

947
01:00:17,030 --> 01:00:18,698
Did he go to my exhibition hall?

948
01:00:23,245 --> 01:00:24,579
[♪ music resumes tempo]

949
01:00:26,039 --> 01:00:27,958
[♪ suspenseful, ominous music playing]

950
01:00:29,417 --> 01:00:30,584
[♪ music swells]

951
01:00:30,585 --> 01:00:31,752
[grunts, exclaims]

952
01:00:31,753 --> 01:00:33,921
- [♪ music increases in tempo]
- [grunts]

953
01:00:33,922 --> 01:00:35,089
[grunts]

954
01:00:35,090 --> 01:00:36,632
- [clattering]
- [panting]

955
01:00:36,633 --> 01:00:37,717
[exhales heavily]

956
01:00:38,426 --> 01:00:40,094
[Isoo] Ah!

957
01:00:40,095 --> 01:00:41,887
I've been looking everywhere for you.

958
01:00:41,888 --> 01:00:43,765
Here you are, making a dramatic entrance.

959
01:00:45,350 --> 01:00:46,518
[both grunting]

960
01:00:49,062 --> 01:00:50,563
- [heavy thud]
- [glass shattering]

961
01:00:50,564 --> 01:00:51,773
[♪ music swells]

962
01:00:53,024 --> 01:00:54,233
[Isoo grunts]

963
01:00:54,234 --> 01:00:55,360
[sighs in relief]

964
01:00:56,027 --> 01:00:57,195
- [sharp whoosh]
- [Isoo exclaims]

965
01:00:57,904 --> 01:00:59,905
[♪ gripping, dramatic music playing]

966
01:00:59,906 --> 01:01:01,449
[both grunting]

967
01:01:07,330 --> 01:01:09,207
[groaning]

968
01:01:10,625 --> 01:01:12,043
- [clatters]
- [Isoo grunts]

969
01:01:13,169 --> 01:01:14,503
[shattering]

970
01:01:14,504 --> 01:01:16,214
[♪ music increases in tempo]

971
01:01:18,758 --> 01:01:20,010
- [Isoo grunts]
- [heavy thud]

972
01:01:24,347 --> 01:01:26,182
[groans]

973
01:01:27,434 --> 01:01:28,851
- [blunt thud]
- [high-pitched ringing]

974
01:01:28,852 --> 01:01:30,061
[thuds]

975
01:01:32,439 --> 01:01:33,772
[distorted thud]

976
01:01:33,773 --> 01:01:35,150
[♪ tense, ominous music playing]

977
01:01:39,696 --> 01:01:41,447
- [hammer clangs]
- [exhales in relief]

978
01:01:41,448 --> 01:01:42,948
[♪ music increases in tempo]

979
01:01:42,949 --> 01:01:43,992
[panting]

980
01:01:48,246 --> 01:01:50,040
[Taeseon's assistant]
<i>Jin Isoo is here inside the studio.</i>

981
01:01:50,832 --> 01:01:51,958
Burn him with it.

982
01:01:52,876 --> 01:01:54,961
[liquid splashing]

983
01:01:56,588 --> 01:01:58,632
[♪ gripping, foreboding music playing]

984
01:02:05,221 --> 01:02:06,222
[lighter clicks open]

985
01:02:08,683 --> 01:02:10,101
[♪ music increases in tempo]

986
01:02:42,300 --> 01:02:43,384
[♪ music fades]

987
01:02:43,385 --> 01:02:44,468
FLEX X COP 2
EPISODE 13

988
01:02:44,469 --> 01:02:45,886
WHAT FATE AWAITS ISOO?

989
01:02:45,887 --> 01:02:47,597
[♪ upbeat pop music playing]

990
01:03:20,964 --> 01:03:22,089
[Hyera] Chief.

991
01:03:22,090 --> 01:03:23,382
What about Jin Isoo?

992
01:03:23,383 --> 01:03:26,343
You'll wake up, right?
I know you won't let this break you.

993
01:03:26,344 --> 01:03:27,720
Jin Isoo is still alive.

994
01:03:27,721 --> 01:03:29,388
When it's done, leave the country.

995
01:03:29,389 --> 01:03:31,974
[Taeseon's assistant] <i>The basement
was destroyed. We won't find any evidence.</i>

996
01:03:31,975 --> 01:03:34,519
He's on the move with Yu Seongwon.
We're following them.

997
01:03:35,854 --> 01:03:37,521
[Hyera] Detective Park! Detective Choi!

998
01:03:37,522 --> 01:03:39,398
Yu Seongwon's gone. He ditched the car.

999
01:03:39,399 --> 01:03:41,109
There's no choice. I'll finish this.

1000
01:03:41,985 --> 01:03:44,695
Do you get it now?
This is the death you love so much.

1001
01:03:44,696 --> 01:03:46,280
[laughing maniacally]

1002
01:03:46,281 --> 01:03:47,448
[Isoo] Yu Seongwon!

1003
01:03:47,449 --> 01:03:48,450
<i>You crazy bastard.</i>

1004
01:03:50,827 --> 01:03:51,953
[♪ music fades]

1005
01:03:54,164 --> 01:03:55,582
[♪ suspenseful, ominous music playing]

1006
01:03:55,749 --> 01:03:59,877
NUMBER 1 SAFETY!! NUMBER 1 PUBLIC ORDER!!
GANGHA POLICE STATION

1007
01:03:59,878 --> 01:04:00,879
[sighs softly]

1008
01:04:02,756 --> 01:04:03,798
[scoffs softly]

1009
01:04:07,218 --> 01:04:09,095
[♪ somber, ominous music playing]

1010
01:04:23,193 --> 01:04:24,235
[exhales softly]

1011
01:05:05,819 --> 01:05:07,362
Should I just disappear?

1012
01:05:09,072 --> 01:05:10,115
[scoffs softly]

1013
01:05:11,199 --> 01:05:13,784
Should I make one final piece?

1014
01:05:13,785 --> 01:05:15,078
[♪ music swells]

1015
01:05:18,748 --> 01:05:19,832
[♪ music fades]

1016
01:05:19,833 --> 01:05:21,835
Translated by Hyesoo Lee
